<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 70,346 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 70,346 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 70,346 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday compared to 65,056 tonnes in the same period on Sunday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Monday	June 29</p>
<p>    Export cargo		10,287	29,156</p>
<p>    Import cargo		60,059	35,900</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, seven ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, three are expected to sail and 10 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Gas oil		60,000	 CSP-10		     1/7</p>
<p>Crude oil	    66,000	 Johar			1/7</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
